#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096653 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector That Satisfies a Ratio in Terms of Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "747da426-8469-5cfb-b9c1-0f275aa12f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{1}{4}a+\\frac{3}{4}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420450} {:answer/id #uuid "7870ed39-d3a3-5476-9037-af3a46374a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{5}{8}a+\\frac{3}{8}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420451} {:answer/id #uuid "ac24f6e2-146b-56c4-926e-7b7b203e75f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{3}{8}a+\\frac{5}{8}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420454} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a4f00d-a543-5fec-976f-fd2b59d619f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{3}{4}a+\\frac{1}{4}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420458} {:answer/id #uuid "f78f9d21-45cd-5cd7-95b8-055e70bef457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{7}{8}a+\\frac{1}{8}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7870ed39-d3a3-5476-9037-af3a46374a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\frac{5}{8}a+\\frac{3}{8}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420451} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cd7bc1d-4953-5e13-8ab6-2c158bebc612" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fe46ce7-a162-566e-a261-116569794a12" :question/math-academy-id "q-120289" :question/problem "![](images/52/52e25ccc5b59b3eecd914c5b141e443475a5de58299404528d27f1fc85db97ea.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OB}=b$, and $T$ divides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ in the ratio $AT:TB=3:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OT}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-a+b \\\\  & =b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AT:TB=3:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AT}=\\frac{3}{8}\\overset{\\to }{AB}=\\frac{3}{8}(b-a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AT} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{3}{8}(b-a) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}a+\\frac{3}{8}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096652 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Scalar Factors in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f1fbbe3-94d8-5bd3-8727-4e6f9a832097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420448} {:answer/id #uuid "90599886-7bfb-5b72-84ac-b60df87c5d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420452} {:answer/id #uuid "a6826047-3513-5e97-9ed8-1ae795633fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420453} {:answer/id #uuid "b05969db-3a13-5b96-96be-8b739e33d310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420455} {:answer/id #uuid "cf620219-7b28-5e23-a450-b4abd046ba47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6826047-3513-5e97-9ed8-1ae795633fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420453} :answer-field/id #uuid "979e9c27-4560-5e47-8337-19ce5dc8192c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5f98ecb-0f26-50ae-9a82-cc334fd82c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-20413" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4bb7598c9ebae28be572508974cd025caa8f4a6c3313f025ff0f5ca55296334e.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $h=\\lambda f+\\mu g$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/43/43642acdb991827b4e1e16744e8a69507a383a1319ae07efde78480af4bab166.png)\n\nIn $△OFH$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OF=2|g|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OF}$ and $g$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=2g.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $FH=3|f|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FH}$ has the opposite direction to $f$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{FH}=-3f.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FH} \\\\  & =2g-3f \\\\  & =-3f+2g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $h=\\lambda f+\\mu g=-3f+2g.$\n\nSince $f∦g,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fbb8f19-f35a-59c4-9b77-8f6c3542ef28" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Scalar Factor in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271316bb-de9b-5d8b-bad0-ffd1bfc5b101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420447} {:answer/id #uuid "633d97e3-8d84-57c9-8ac7-bdd2378d9d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420449} {:answer/id #uuid "c2051bdd-22cb-509c-8fb6-340e90eb858d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420456} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4325a-2b33-5c98-a020-248e21f996f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420459} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d19e05-07c5-5adc-9a1c-131ee586eacd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "271316bb-de9b-5d8b-bad0-ffd1bfc5b101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420447} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f94aaa-a8cf-5aa4-9f93-884e35c10a15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b667d36f-710b-5326-b636-9597ec1ec3f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-77230" :question/problem "![](images/8c/8cf7d0520b1d0654d5749651595acd48b7a08f2b2d55142b18ca63b2ded20f55.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+2b$, find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/9e/9edea1e3ad727d11d7bfac884f27c1b435233fa7df561dbe2a4f3af45ea16bfa.png)\n\nIn $△OBC$, we have:\n\n- $BC=3|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{BC}=3a.$ \n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}+\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & =2b+3a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=2b+\\lambda a=2b+3a.$ \n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =3\n$$"}]}
